let __v_307 = Value::from("Report it the same day - 101 or the police's own online form - and give the frame number, which is stamped under the bottom bracket and is what the police and any insurer check a found bike against. Then list it as stolen on BikeRegister or 529 Garage, because a bike that turns up is matched through them, and ring your home contents insurer: most policies cover a bike taken away from home if it was locked to something fixed, and the claim wants the report number and the receipt or a photo. Watch the local selling sites for a few days.");
frame.store("STOLEN_THING_BIKE", __v_307.clone())?;
let __v_308 = Value::from("Report it on 101 the same day and keep the crime reference number, then ring the insurer of the van and any separate tools cover: tools carried for work are often on a different policy to the vehicle, and both want a list with serial numbers, photos and receipts. Photograph the broken lock or window before anything is repaired, tell the employer if the tools were theirs, and ask the insurer before replacing a big-ticket tool, because some settle at the trade price.");
frame.store("STOLEN_THING_TOOLS", __v_308.clone())?;
let __v_309 = Value::from("Until a parcel reaches you it is the retailer's problem, not yours: tell them it never arrived, or that it was left outside and taken, and ask for a replacement or a refund - you did not choose the courier. Photograph the empty doorstep and the tracking page, check with the neighbours and anywhere a courier hides things first, and if the retailer refuses, a card chargeback is the next step, since a card payment protects you for goods not received. Ask the retailer to send the next one to a locker or with a signature.");
frame.store("STOLEN_THING_PARCEL", __v_309.clone())?;
let __v_310 = Value::from("Report it on 101 and keep the crime reference number, then ring your home contents insurer: an item taken from the house, the car or a bag is usually covered, and the claim wants the serial number or a photo and the receipt. For a laptop, camera or watch, sign out of the accounts on it remotely and change the password on your main email, because that is the key to everything else. If it was taken in a burglary, do not tidy up before the police or the insurer have seen it.");
frame.store("STOLEN_THING_GEAR", __v_310.clone())?;
