let __v_392 = Value::from("Report it to HM Passport Office as soon as you know it is gone, so it is cancelled and cannot be used, and report it to the police as well - keep the crime reference. If you need to travel soon, ask the Passport Office about an emergency travel document or the fast-track service rather than waiting for a new one. The carrier's claim covers only what the posting cost, not the passport fee, so start the replacement the same day.");
frame.store("_PASSPORT_CLAIM", __v_392.clone())?;
let __v_393 = Value::from("Find the proof of posting - the receipt from the counter or the drop-off, or the emailed label and its barcode - because that is what a claim rests on. Then open a claim with the carrier you handed it to, not the shop: Royal Mail keeps a lost item claim open from 10 working days after posting up to 80 days, and pays what the service covers - about £20 on standard with proof of posting, £50 on Signed For, more on Special Delivery, so check the cover before you count on it. Put the value and receipts in the claim, and if the item was tracked, add the tracking number to it. A card or a letter goes the same way.");
frame.store("_PARCEL_CLAIM", __v_393.clone())?;
