let __v_3217 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"intestate\",\"intestacy\",\"died intestate\",\"dies intestate\",\"no will\",\"without a will\",\"died without a will\"]},\"If someone dies intestate they died without a valid will, so the law decides who gets what. In England and Wales a spouse or civil partner gets the personal possessions and the first £322,000, with the rest shared with the children; partners who were not married get nothing without a will. The court appoints an administrator where a will would have named an executor.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tenancy agreement\",\"tenancy contract\",\"renting agreement\",\"assured shorthold\",\"ast tenancy\",\"shorthold tenancy\"]},\"A tenancy agreement is the contract between you and the landlord: it sets the rent, how long the tenancy runs, who pays which bills, who repairs what, and whether you can have a pet or sublet. An assured shorthold tenancy is the ordinary kind for a private renter in England - a fixed term (often 12 months) and then a rolling monthly one - and since 2019 the landlord must give you the government's How to Rent guide and a current gas safety certificate before you move in. It is a contract, so read the clauses on repairs and notice before you sign, and keep a copy: the landlord has to provide one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"a will\",\"the will\",\"my will\",\"his will\",\"her will\",\"their will\",\"your will\",\"last will\",\"last will and testament\",\"wills\",\"write a will\",\"make a will\"]},\"A will says who gets what when you die, and who sorts it out - the executor. It only counts if it is signed and witnessed by two people who are not beneficiaries, and the last valid one wins, so tell the executor where it is kept. Without one the law shares the estate out by fixed rules, which may not be what you would choose.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"executor\",\"executors\",\"executrix\"]},\"An executor is the person named in a will to carry it out: register the death with the will, apply for probate, value the estate, pay the debts and inheritance tax, then share out what is left. You can be one without any legal training, and many people do it themselves; a solicitor is worth paying for if there is a house, a business or a disagreement.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"beneficiary\",\"beneficiaries\"]},\"A beneficiary is a person or an organisation named to receive something - in a will, an insurance policy or a pension. Being named in a will does not override a pension or insurance form, so the nomination held by the pension firm is what pays out, and it is worth checking after a divorce or a death.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"next of kin\"]},\"Next of kin means your nearest relative, and hospitals and banks ask for it as the person to ring. It does not give that person the right to make decisions for an adult: medical decisions are the doctor's with the patient, and money decisions need lasting power of attorney. A partner who is not married can be next of kin if you say so in writing.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"deed poll\",\"change my name deed poll\"]},\"A deed poll is the one-page document you sign to change your own name: it costs nothing to write yourself, and enrolling it with the Royal Courts of Justice for about £42 makes it easier for banks and passport offices to accept. You can use the new name straight away; the passport, driving licence and bank are the ones to change first.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"statutory declaration\",\"statutory declarations\"]},\"A statutory declaration is a written statement that you sign in front of a solicitor or a magistrate and swear is true - commonly used to prove a change of name, a lost document or a fact you cannot evidence another way. It is not free: a solicitor charges about £5 to £15 for the signature, and you need to take the wording with you.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"solicitor\",\"solicitors\",\"lawyer\",\"lawyers\"]},\"A solicitor is a lawyer who advises you and prepares the documents: a house purchase, a will, a dispute, a crime. In England and Wales they must be regulated by the SRA or the Law Society and carry insurance, which is what to check on the firm's number before you pay. The first appointment is often free, and a fixed fee is normal for a will or a conveyance.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ccj\",\"ccjs\",\"county court judgment\",\"county court judgements\",\"county court judgments\"]},\"A CCJ is a county court judgment: a court has ruled that you owe someone money, and the judgment appears on your credit file for six years. Pay it in full within a month of the post arriving and you can ask the court to remove it; after that it is marked satisfied, which still shows. If you cannot pay, apply to the court to pay by instalments rather than ignore it, because ignoring it is what leads to bailiffs.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"affidavit\",\"affidavits\"]},\"An affidavit is a written statement of evidence that you swear in front of a solicitor or court officer. Most of the places that used to ask for one now accept a statement of truth, which you sign without the fee - so ask which one the form really wants before you pay for a signature.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"notary\",\"notaries\",\"notary public\"]},\"A notary public is a lawyer who certifies documents for use in another country: they check who you are, watch you sign, and seal it so the foreign authority accepts it. Banks and embassies abroad usually ask for it, it costs £50 to £150 a document, and a solicitor can find you one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lien\",\"liens\"]},\"A lien is a legal claim that a lender or a tradesman holds on your property until a debt is paid: a mortgage is a lien on the house, and a garage can keep your car until its bill is settled. It does not usually change who owns the thing, but it can stop a sale, so a letter mentioning one is worth answering.\"]}]}")?;
